  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID-Amphibians In Decline</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;AD-0135: Identifying disease risk in threatened amphibians in the Itombwe and Misotshi-Kabogo massifs, Democratic Republic of Congo. In partnership with the Wildlife Conservation Society (WCS), this project will support a conservation effort for multiple amphibian species in the Itombwe and Misotshi-Kabogo massifs of eastern Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC), by determining the prevalence of amphibian diseases in the field and in specimens collected in the past..Specific activities include: (1) field surveys of chytrid fungus and ranavirus at 12 sites in Itombwe and Misotshi-Kabogo, including an anticipated 250 individual frogs; (2) laboratory tests of skin and tissue samples at the WCS molecular lab in New York, or the WCS Mobile Molecular Laboratory in DRC; (3) laboratory tests of archived amphibian specimens for chytrid fungus through histological (tissue) analysis to establish a baseline for disease monitoring; and (4) a map and model of disease distribution in relation to habitat and ecology in the broader Albertine Rift region.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
